  "title": "Graeme C NDE 7135",
  "date": "19 February 2014",
  "content": "I suffer with (normally) well-controlled asthma. However, the asthma is currently exacerbated by a sinus and lung infection. This has led to severe bouts of uncontrollable coughing. During one of the coughing fits, I appeared to pass out, stop breathing and had to be revived by my wife. I apparently suffered no ill effects. A little later the same evening, whilst watching TV on my own, I had another severe coughing fit. Since there was no one around to revive me, I guess the fit ran its full course and I must have stopped breathing. It was then that I sensed the sweet perfume of incense and found myself looking into a brightly lit, white-walled corridor. I remember feeling very calm and not at all afraid. I think the experience lasted a brief few seconds before my breathing started and I came around. The whole experience, whilst not at all unpleasant was, nevertheless, quite perturbing. As you will already have realized, I have no really positive thoughts about religion or the afterlife. However this experience has made me think again.",
